      <!-- WHAT THE COURT HANDLES -->
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="overview-heading">
        <h2 id="overview-heading">What the Dubai Personal Status Court Handles</h2>
        <p>
          Dubai has no court officially called the "family court". Family matters go to the
          <strong>Personal Status Court</strong> of Dubai Courts, which sits with the Inheritance Court.
          It deals with marriage (the 2024 law requires a marriage contract to be documented in court,
          Article 41), divorce and khula, the documenting of a talaq, custody and visitation, alimony and
          child maintenance, dowry claims, court permits such as permission for a custodial parent to
          travel abroad with a child (Article 116), and inheritance and wills.
        </p>
        <p>
          UAE courts hear personal status cases against citizens and foreigners who have a domicile,
          residence or place of work in the UAE (Article 3 of Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2024). For
          divorce, khula, alimony, custody, visitation and dowry claims brought by a wife, children,
          parents or a custodian, the case can go to the court where the plaintiff or the respondent
          lives or works, or where the marital home is. The Dubai Courts claim service also expects one party to be a
          citizen or resident of Dubai.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two laws run through the same court:
        </p>
        <ul class="list">
          <li><strong>Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2024</strong> on Personal Status, in force since 15 April 2025, for Muslims. It also covers foreigners in general unless one spouse insists on applying their own national law (Article 1).</li>
          <li><strong>Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2022</strong> on Civil Personal Status, in force since 1 February 2023, for non-Muslim UAE nationals and non-Muslim foreigners living in the UAE, unless one spouse holds to the law of their home country (Article 1).</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="summary-box">
          <h3>Quick Reference</h3>
          <div class="summary-grid">
            <div class="summary-item">
              <span class="label">Court name</span>
